@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# RCTP - Taiwan Taoyuan International Airport
+
+## About this facility
+
+Taiwan Taoyuan International Airport is the primary international airport for northern Taiwan and the main hub for China Airlines, EVA Air, Starlux Airlines, and Tigerair Taiwan.
+
+The first openScope version uses real-world annual traffic volume as the traffic target. Public 2025 statistics list 262,217 aircraft movements, which is about 30 aircraft per hour when averaged across a full year. In the airport load list this places RCTP in the `easy` traffic bucket.
+
+## Positions
+
+| Callsign | Remarks |
+|----------|---------|
+| Taoyuan Tower | Runway and local airport control |
+| Taipei Approach | Arrival sequencing into Taoyuan |
+| Taipei Departure | Initial climb and departure flow |
+
+## Runways
+
+RCTP has two parallel runways:
+
+| Runway pair | Use in this file |
+|-------------|------------------|
+| 05L / 23R | Primary arrival/departure-capable runway |
+| 05R / 23L | Parallel arrival/departure-capable runway |
+
+This first pass defaults to eastbound operations with arrivals on 05L and departures on 05R.
+
+## Instrument Procedures
+
+The current file provides four simplified traffic corridors: north, east, south, and west. These corridors are intended to make the airport playable while keeping the data easy to replace with exact Taiwan CAA / Taipei FIR eAIP procedure data.
+
+## Terrain
+
+RCTP includes a sea-level water polygon for the northern Taiwan coastline plus an SRTM-derived terrain layer clipped to the local control area. The elevated terrain is simplified into OpenScope's 1000 ft display bands, which captures the high ground east and southeast of Taoyuan without making the airport asset too large.
+
+## Traffic
+
+The active live spawn model is tuned to 30 arrival aircraft per hour in this arrival-only checkout. This matches the real-world annual-average traffic target while avoiding inactive departure spawn patterns.
+
+The airline options follow the local RJTT simulation style: each arrival corridor uses a compact carrier list weighted toward home operators. Regional flows use EVA Air, China Airlines, Starlux Airlines, and Tigerair Taiwan; long-haul flows use the long-haul fleets for EVA Air, China Airlines, and Starlux Airlines.
+
+## Additional Resources
+
+Use the Taiwan CAA / Taipei FIR eAIP as the authoritative source for future runway-threshold, SID, STAR, airspace, and chart refinements.
